A||N||4||WhiteFieroBlur||Burning and steering trouble||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||06-12-2000||11:12 AM||||I drive down the street and after a while I start to smell something burning behind my left front tire. Also the sterring on the left side pulls to the left. I have to hold the wheel straight or if I let go, I am going right into the left lane. The steering on the left side is also more loose than the right. Does anyone know what the burning is and how to fix it? And is it bad I have been driving my car like that everyday?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero mistress||06-12-2000||11:37 AM||||I don't know about your steering being loose on the left side...But, it sounds like a sticking caliper to me.<P>We had a sticking caliper on the front passenger side and it caused our '86SE to pull right.  We had to replace the caliper because for ours cleaning and relubricating it didn't work.  I wouldn't drive it that way...it really heats things up with all the friction.  And it will eat up your brake pads in no time flat!<P>Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero mistress (edited 06-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-12-2000||12:29 PM||||The caliper is sticking. The reason it feels loose is because the caliper pulls the steering wheel to that side (less effort)<BR>Replace caliper and inspect rotor and pads.<BR>Rotors can warp under high heat.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||06-12-2000||03:49 PM||||I would look for a sticking caliper first too. DON'T drive it that way, it's a dangerous situation. I've seen those rotors get red hot from a dragging caliper. It can even burst the rubber brake hose causing you to have total brake failure. Fix it immediately if not sooner. The longer you wait, the more damage it will cause and the more expensive it will be.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WhiteFieroBlur||06-12-2000||10:11 PM||||Well thanx for all the info, I have been driving it around and I mean cruizing around for a while everyday. I am gonna stop now and call around tomorrow to get it fixed. I didn't know how serious it could be. I hope it isn't too expensive. I can't wait till I get everything fixed on this car, it seems like it wants to make me spend my money. Everyday I fix something and something else pops up. Thanx ||||reg||1
